# Chains of Mephistopheles: "If the player doesn't discard a card this way, they mill a card." With an empty hand there is
# nothing to discard (nobody is asked to choose one), so each of Ancestral Recall's draws becomes a mill of one card and
# "the player doesn't draw a card at all" (its ruling; CR 614.6, 701.17). Bot1 casts everything it holds on turn 1, so its
# hand is empty as Ancestral Recall resolves: the Forest, the Plains and the Mountain on top of its library are milled one at
# a time, and its hand stays empty.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Chains of Mephistopheles
Ancestral Recall
Forest
Plains
Mountain
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chains of Mephistopheles.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
! Bot1.Choose
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Ancestral Recall; Mountain; Plains; Forest
